  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B028",
        "laureates": [
          "Alexander A. Belavin",
          "Alexander B. Zamolodchikov",
          "Alexander M. Polyakov"
        ],
        "citation": "for conformal field theory and its exact description of two-dimensional critical phenomena"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B058",
    "B022"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B028 remains the strongest case for a foundational physical achievement: it supplied a compact and generative account of universality at two-dimensional criticality, joining exact mathematical structure to physical phenomena over decades. Its influence across statistical physics and quantum field theory is not simply broad use of a technique; it changed what could be calculated and understood about critical systems. Belavin, Zamolodchikov, and Polyakov form a coherent attribution to the central theoretical breakthrough.",
    "case_against": "The citation must remain narrowly confined to conformal field theory and exact two-dimensional critical phenomena, rather than claiming the whole subsequent history of conformal methods or quantum field theory. Its theoretical character also requires that its physical explanatory and predictive consequences be made explicit. B058 and B022 offer more immediately delimited experimental or computational achievements with especially clear practical maturity.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll argues that B022 combines Katori's magic-wavelength concept with Ye's defining experimental development in a reproducible and mature precision-measurement platform, while noting that its widest fundamental applications are still developing.",
        "response": "I agree with both the exceptional clarity of the Katori-Ye pairing and the experimental maturity of B022. It remains my leading experimental alternative. But the distinction Kroll identifies matters: lattice clocks are an extraordinarily capable platform, whereas B028 has already provided a long-tested universal explanation of a broad class of physical critical phenomena. I therefore retain B028, subject to rigorous delimitation of its historical scope."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson regards B004 as a coherent union of Kane and Mele's quantum-spin-Hall theory with Molenkamp's experimental realization, while warning that the citation must not subsume the broader history of topological matter.",
        "response": "I share Eriksson's insistence on a narrow achievement boundary, and the same discipline is essential for B028. B004 has a compelling theory-to-experiment narrative, but its relation to the wider development of topological matter leaves its boundary less settled. For B028, the proposed citation can focus specifically on the exact conformal framework for two-dimensional critical phenomena and its three central architects."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson favors B003 because it made squeezing a practical precision-measurement resource, but recognizes unresolved credit among quantum-noise theory, generation, and deployment.",
        "response": "The control of quantum fluctuations in B003 is a profound and mature achievement. Yet the unresolved division of experimental credit is material under the three-person limit. B028 has its own historical-boundary problem, but its central conceptual construction and the proposed three-person attribution are more coherent for the delimited citation."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether a historical review can delimit B028 precisely from related conformal and quantum-field-theoretic developments while preserving the distinctive contribution of each proposed laureate.",
      "Whether the committee should give greater weight to the direct instrumental maturity and compact attribution of B022 or B058 than to B028's established theoretical explanatory power."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "I am at the University of Gothenburg, in the closely linked Gothenburg physics environment with committee colleagues Göran Johansson and Eva Olsson; no specific collaboration with either is apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
